WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.359
The third job is making things better.

2
00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:10.568
Vanderbilt is asking every team to move faster and improve, and that happens in your team, in small ways,

3
00:00:10.618 --> 00:00:14.550
every week. It is not a reorganization. It is four habits.

4
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:19.906
Explain the why: the reason, in your own words, before the announcement lands.

5
00:00:19.956 --> 00:00:21.897
Describe where you are going:

6
00:00:21.947 --> 00:00:27.527
two sentences on what the team will be able to do next year that it cannot do now.

7
00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:30.891
Let people try: small, short trials of new ideas.

8
00:00:30.941 --> 00:00:36.315
Look back: ten minutes after big work. What worked, what did not, what changes.

9
00:00:36.365 --> 00:00:43.593
For example: central is replacing a library’s checkout system in six weeks, and the team has already said,

10
00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:50.184
here we go again. The manager explains the why at her own staff meeting before the campus email,

11
00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:57.324
writes down the hard questions to take back, lets a young staffer test a new cart routine for two weeks,

12
00:00:57.374 --> 00:01:01.100
and holds a ten-minute look-back after move-in weekend.

13
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.778
The team still did not love the system.

14
00:01:03.828 --> 00:01:09.545
But they heard the why from her first, and two of them volunteered to test it early.

15
00:01:09.595 --> 00:01:12.360
This week: hold one ten-minute look-back.

